  "content": [
    {
      "text": "the Messiah is full of grace and truth, 2 Ne. 2:6 (Alma 5:48; 9:26; 13:9). O wisdom of God, his mercy and grace, 2 Ne. 9:8. because of grace and mercy, the Lord has promised that Nephites’ seed shall not be destroyed, 2 Ne. 9:53. only in and through grace of God that men are saved, 2 Ne. 10:24. my soul delighteth in the Lord’s grace, 2 Ne. 11:5. by grace we are saved, after all we can do, 2 Ne. 25:23. the Lord showeth us our weakness that we may know it is by his grace that we have power, Jacob 4:7. people of Alma1 are baptized and filled with grace of God, Mosiah 18:16. for their labor priests were to receive grace of God, Mosiah 18:26 (27:5). continue in supplicating of the Lord’s grace, Alma 7:3. men should repent that they might be restored unto grace for grace, Hel. 12:24. day of grace is past with Nephites, Morm. 2:15. the Lord’s grace is sufficient for meek, Ether 12:26–27. Moroni2 prays the Lord will give Gentiles grace, Ether 12:36, 41. by grace of the Father and Christ, Mormon2 is permitted to speak, Moro. 7:2. continually praying that God, through infinite grace, will keep you, Moro. 8:3. ye may be perfect in Christ, by his grace, Moro. 10:32–33.",
